&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Joining Capco means joining an organization that is committed to an inclusive working environment where you’re encouraged to #BeYourselfAtWork. We celebrate individuality and recognize that diversity and inclusion, in all forms, is critical to success. It’s important to us that we recruit and develop as diverse a range of talent as we can and we believe that everyone brings something different to the table – so we’d love to know what makes you different. Such differences may mean we need to make changes to our process to allow you the best possible platform to succeed, and we are happy to cater to any reasonable adjustments you may require. You will find the section to let us know of these at the bottom of your application form or you can mention it directly to your recruiter at any stage and they will be happy to help.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Capco&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Capco is a global technology and management consultancy dedicated to the financial services industry. We combine innovative thinking with unrivalled industry knowledge, to offer our clients consulting expertise, complex technology and package integration, transformation delivery and managed services to move their organizations forward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We specialize primarily in banking &amp;amp; payments, capital markets, wealth &amp;amp; asset management, insurance and energy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have a collaborative and efficient approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We help our clients successfully innovate, increase revenue, manage risk and regulatory change, reduce costs and enhance controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We serve our clients from 32 offices across the Americas, Europe, and Asia Pacific&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If creativity and innovation are your passion, then Capco is right for you. You can grow in an inclusive, diverse and collaborative environment. At Capco, we will train and support you to help accelerate your career.&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW202573807 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior / Principal Consultant, you will play a key role in the functional design and further development of modern Management Reporting and Management Information Systems for Retail Banking, Corporate Banking, Private Banking, Wealth Management and Asset Management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Acting as a Business Functional Analyst at the intersection of Business, Data, and IT, you will ensure that business requirements are translated into sustainable management reporting and steering solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will advise our clients on defining banking KPIs, enhancing reporting processes, and modernizing existing MIS landscapes. In addition to contributing your functional expertise, you will actively support client development, project management, and the continued development of our Banking Consulting capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR CAPCO DAY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise local and international banks on the development and enhancement of Management Information Systems and reporting landscapes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take functional ownership as a Business Functional Analyst, working across Business, Data, and IT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, harmonize, and further develop banking KPIs for Retail Banking, Corporate Banking, Private Banking, Wealth Management and Asset Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex business requirements into functional concepts, reporting logic, and functional requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze and optimize reporting processes and data journeys across the entire reporting value chain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and facilitate workshops with business divisions/functions and senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support testing, KPI validation, and the implementation of new reporting solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR CAPCO FIT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5–6 years of experience in consulting or in a business function within a private bank&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience in Reporting and Management Information Systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth understanding of products and processes within Retail Banking, Corporate Banking, Private Banking, Wealth Management and/or Asset Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a Business Analyst or Functional Analyst in regulatory or business transformation projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Very good knowledge of banking KPIs, management reporting, and sales steering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Business, Data, and IT stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience facilitating workshops and managing stakeholders at management level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and structured approach, combined with well-developed consulting skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in German and English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NICE TO HAVE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience transforming global reporting and MIS landscapes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience migrating MIS and reporting systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of cloud data platforms and modern BI architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing stakeholders at senior/executive management level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHY CAPCO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A career at Capco is a chance to help reshape the competitive landscape in financial services. We launch new banks, transform existing ones, and help our clients navigate complex change. As consultants, we work on the front-end business design all the way through to technology implementation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are the largest Financial Services focused consultancy in the world, serving everyone from global banks to emerging FinTechs, from strategy through digital transformation, design, business consulting, data and analytics, cyber, cloud, technology architecture, and engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Capco is a young and growing firm. We maintain an entrepreneurial spirit and growth mindset, and have minimal bureaucracy. We have no internal silos that get in the way of your career opportunities or ability to focus on our clients and make a difference to the business. We offer the opportunity for everyone to learn rapidly, take on tough challenges, and get promoted quickly. We take pride in our creative, collaborative, diverse, and inclusive culture, where everyone can #BYAW.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer highly competitive benefits, flexible working hours, technical and soft skills training, smartphone &amp;amp; fast mobile internet and a work culture focused on innovation and creation of lasting value for our clients and employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ready to take the Next Step&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this sounds like you, we would love to hear from you. &amp;nbsp;This is an opportunity to make a difference and contribute to a highly successful company with a significant growth trajectory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;sc-gEkIjz cjtSrT MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 sc-hoLEA&quot;&gt;Raisin is the world’s leading platform for savings and investment products. Founded in 2012, the&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;FinTech&lt;/strong&gt; connects consumers with banks in the EU, the UK and the US. This gives consumers &lt;strong&gt;better interest rates&lt;/strong&gt; and banks a &lt;strong&gt;diversified form of refinancing&lt;/strong&gt;. Our vision is to offer savings and investments without barriers and thus open up the global 160 trillion euro market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;sc-gEkIjz cjtSrT MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 sc-hoLEA&quot;&gt;Raisin currently employs more than 800 people from over 75 countries worldwide. Today, the platform holds over 80 billion euros in assets from&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;more than one million investors&lt;/strong&gt; which have accrued over 5 billion euros in returns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The People Solutions team serves as the strategic engine room of Raisin’s People &amp;amp; Culture team by building a secure, data-driven, and compliant infrastructure that scales the organization. By bridging the gap between strategy and technology, the team optimizes HRIS systems to eliminate manual work, leverages analytics and AI to drive smarter business decisions, and acts as a compliance anchor managing audits, policies, and risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Your Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;We are looking for a Senior People Application Manager to own the administration, architecture, and strategic optimization of Raisin’s People applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;You will ensure smooth operations of the HRIS and its connected applications and be the final point of escalation for incident resolution across our People tooling stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;You will lead the configuration of Raisin’s People applications to meet evolving business needs based on the complex requirements of the People business functions and in close alignment with the People Solutions leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;You will own and optimize the automated account onboarding, lifecycle workflows, and IAM strategy of the People applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;You will drive seamless, scalable integrations of Raisin’s People applications in close alignment with People Solutions leadership and other stakeholders such as the Enterprise IT and Security teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;You will establish governance and own the documentation of configuration, customisation, and interface architecture of Raisin’s People applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Your Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;You hold a university degree in Computer Science, or a related field, or bring equivalent experience with a strong analytical background.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;You have 5+ years of hands-on experience in application management, systems engineering, or IT leadership in the People domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;You are able to design and manage incident response frameworks, tasks, and system uptime within enterprise SLAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;You have deep, end-to-end People domain knowledge including complex People processes and data models across the entire employee lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;You are highly responsible, trustworthy, and adept at establishing data privacy standards and handling sensitive and confidential data with the utmost discretion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;You have exceptional communication skills and you feel comfortable collaborating with and influencing both technical, executive, and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;You are fluent in English (German would be a plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Proven expertise with modern HRIS tooling stacks (especially Personio or enterprise SaaS platforms) is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join our mission, join our team – and grow with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Raisin, we care about each other and it is one of our top priorities to foster an open and caring environment in which everyone feels welcome and comfortable. Our culture is strongly driven by our ambitious team, which connects more than 75 different nationalities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of our team, you will benefit from&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Development Budget of €2,000 and four full training days per year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours, home office and 30 vacation days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A company pension scheme (Betriebliche Altersvorsorge), which we support with 20%.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy more than 50+ different sports with Urban Sports Club: We subsidise your membership with more than €20 per month.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do you miss being in the office? The Deutschland Ticket gets you there, which we subsidise with €25 per month.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Love cycling? With JobRad, lease the bike of your choice and enjoy tax savings, plus Raisin covers your monthly insurance costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hungry all the time? Snacks, daily fresh fruit as well as drinks provided at the office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are moving from another country or city to join us? We may support your relocation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.raisin.com/corporate/raisin-applicant-privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Raisin Applicant Privacy Policy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;728&quot; data-end=&quot;900&quot;&gt;We value diversity and the unique experiences each individual brings. If you’re excited about this role but don’t meet every requirement, we still encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;907&quot; data-end=&quot;1013&quot;&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for everyone, regardless of race, colour, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, or gender identity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Robotics &amp;amp; Mechatronics Teams at Agile Robots&lt;/strong&gt; are looking for a&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;C++ Software Engineer (m/f/d) Platform Infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt;, who will help build and maintain the C++ platform infrastructure our robot runs on. You will help us ensure it runs reliably and safely once it is out of the lab and in production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and maintain modern C++ software components for the robot&#39;s Linux-based platform infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; IPC:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and maintain the IPC and communication interfaces that connect robot applications, backend services, and hardware-facing components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Debugging &amp;amp; Diagnostics:&lt;/strong&gt; Debug concurrency, timing, memory, performance, and system-integration issues across the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Testing Infrastructure:&lt;/strong&gt; Build unit, integration, and hardware-oriented test infrastructure for platform components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reliability &amp;amp; Observability:&lt;/strong&gt; Improve system reliability through better diagnostics, logging, fault handling, and recovery mechanisms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hardware Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Test and integrate software on real robotic hardware, working with firmware, control, backend, QA, and DevOps engineers when problems cross those boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Background:&lt;/strong&gt; Degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of training and experience, with initial professional experience building production C++ software, typically up to about three years and excluding internships or working-student positions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Modern C++:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience writing C++ using modern practices (C++17/C++20), gained through professional work, internships, or substantial project experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems Programming:&lt;/strong&gt; Working understanding of Linux system programming — processes, threads, synchronization, IPC, and sockets — along with asynchronous programming concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Debugging:&lt;/strong&gt; Practical debugging experience using tools such as GDB, sanitizers (ASan/TSan/UBSan), or Valgrind, applied to problems that span multiple interacting software or hardware components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Testing:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience writing automated tests with frameworks such as GoogleTest, including meaningful unit and integration test coverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beneficial Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Robotics &amp;amp; Industrial Background:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with robotics, industrial automation, or embedded systems, including industrial communication protocols such as EtherCAT, CAN, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hardware-in-the-Loop Testing:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with hardware-in-the-loop, simulation, fault-injection, or other automated system-testing approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Embedded Linux:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with real-time or performance-sensitive Linux systems, or with the deployment side of embedded Linux.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Python Tooling:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience using Python for testing, automation, or developer tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Assisted Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience using AI-assisted development tools, combined with critically reviewing and validating the generated output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;TranslationField-module__fieldItemName___Q0F_7 TranslationField-module__aboutUsWrapper___WXJpq&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;A dynamic high-tech company, combined with financial soundness and world-class investors.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Join an interdisciplinary, international team with 60+ different nationalities in a collaborative work environment.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Lots of development opportunities as we continue to grow.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Challenging tasks and impactful projects alongside experts that enable professional and personal growth.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Corporate Benefits Program covering health, mobility, and learning for 100€ net per month.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Modern office facilities with a rooftop terrace overlooking Munich, free drinks &amp;amp; fruits, and regular company events contribute to a good working environment&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;TranslationField-module__fieldItemValue___c0djd&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agile Robots SE&lt;/strong&gt; is an international high-tech company based in Munich, Germany with a production site in Kaufbeuren and more than &lt;strong&gt;3500&lt;/strong&gt; employees worldwide. Our mission is to bridge the gap between artificial intelligence and robotics by developing systems that combine state-of-the-art force-moment-sensing and world-leading image-processing technology. This unique combination of technologies allows us to provide user-friendly and affordable robotic solutions that enable intelligent precision assembly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is made possible by our employees, who bring out the best in each and every day with creativity and enthusiasm. Become part of this team and shape the future of robotics with us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud of our diversity and welcome your application regardless of gender and sexual identity, nationality, ethnicity, religion, age, or disability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of Position&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Awin&#39;s Unlock the Clock (UTC) programme is building the evidence base and infrastructure to move measurement beyond last click, using deterministic, CDN/edge-level signals and advanced data connections from publishers to show the full-funnel and AI-discovery influence that today&#39;s attribution misses. The value of that dataset scales with the quality and scale of the publishers inside it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role exists to acquire and retain those publishers. The Senior Partnerships Manager, Media &amp;amp; Data owns the end-to-end pursuit of medium-to-large global media publications and publisher groups, from first conversation to signature, to live, verified data flowing, and is responsible for building the commercial value exchange that makes Awin the leading partner for a premium publisher to work with. The focus in year one is a small number of flagship, tier-one lighthouse partnerships that prove the model and become the reference cases the rest of the market follows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a new, dedicated role. It is not general publisher account management: the postholder is hired to spearhead these relationships and nothing else.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Land flagship media partnerships&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and own a global target list of medium-to-large media publications and publisher groups whose audience, content and commerce activity make them high-value contributors to Awin’s deterministic dataset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full pursuit cycle for those targets: identify, qualify, pitch, negotiate, close and hand into onboarding, personally leading senior conversations with commercial, ecommerce, editorial and digital leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver a defined number of tier-one lighthouse partnerships in year one: signed tracking addendum, technically onboarded, and verifiably recording events at agreed volume and quality thresholds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Convert those wins into reference cases, including case studies, joint narratives and referenceable contacts, that materially shorten the sales cycle for the next tranche of publishers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the publisher value proposition&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and continuously sharpen the answer to “what’s in it for the publisher”: the commercial, editorial and strategic reasons a premium media owner shares CDN and wider data signals with Awin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Construct and negotiate the value exchange, including new revenue lines, advertiser demand, insight and benchmarking, or commercial terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product, Marketing and the workstream owners to translate AI-visibility and full-funnel capability into publisher-facing propositions, collateral and retailer pricing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help each partner build their own value proposition, so the publisher has something new and differentiated to sell to advertisers, not simply a new tag on their site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equip partners to sell that proposition through joint collateral, benchmarks, proof points and training for their commercial and editorial teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed publisher objections, commercial expectations and market intelligence back into the project roadmap so the product earns the deals rather than the deals stretching the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the technical and contractual path to live&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the integration conversation with publishes, covering CDN/edge worker or plugin deployment, tag and consent implications, data scope and page performance, with Awin product brought in for deep technical detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the commercial and legal process end to end, including tracking addendum, data-sharing terms, privacy and consent positions, working with Legal and Privacy to reach repeatable rather than bespoke agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold partners accountable to going live and staying live, tracking signed-to-verified-event conversion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global reach and internal leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate globally from day one across UK, EU and US, coordinating with local Awin market and Publisher Development teams and identified regional representatives rather than duplicating them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the single point of accountability and internal voice for media partner acquisition within the project: represent the workstream in relevant forums and provide clear, honest pipeline and progress reporting to SteerCo level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the advertiser-facing teams so publisher supply and advertiser demand are sequenced together: the data has to be sold on as well as signed up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Awin externally at key industry events, conferences and partner forums to promote Unlock the Clock and Awin’s fuller-funnel measurement strategy to the media community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the playbook: document what works, so the model can be scaled by others and, in time, by a small team reporting into this role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Success measures (first 12 months)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Signed and live tier-one lighthouse partnerships against an agreed target, evidenced by verified event volume&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A qualified, weighted global pipeline of medium-to-large media groups with credible forward visibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A repeatable publisher proposition and commercial framework: not a series of bespoke negotiations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner-facing value propositions live in market, with at least two partners actively selling an Awin-enabled proposition of their own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Referenceable partners willing to advocate publicly, at least one flagship case study in market, and Awin represented on stage at relevant industry events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measurable advertiser-side pull-through from the partnerships landed, agreed jointly with the advertiser teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in commercial, partnership or account leadership roles, with a significant portion earned publisher-side or media-owner-side.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An established personal network of senior contacts across the media and publishing world that can be activated from day one. This is a prerequisite, not a nice-to-have.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience representing an organisation publicly: speaking at industry events, on panels or at partner forums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable track record of senior-level relationships inside premium publishers or media groups, including commercial directors, heads of ecommerce, editorial and digital leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience negotiating and closing commercial agreements with, or on behalf of, publishers: tenancy, CPC, CPA, fixed fee, data or licensing deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of the affiliate and performance ecosystem and how publishers monetise content, for example Awin, Skimlinks, Rakuten, Partnerize, Impact or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling or landing something new, a product, model or proposition without an established category, rather than managing an existing book of business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable navigating multi-stakeholder deals spanning commercial, editorial, legal, privacy and technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International exposure across at least two of UK, US and DACH/EMEA markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desirable: experience with content licensing, AI/LLM discovery, SEO/AEO, or data partnership deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercially creative, able to construct a value exchange where no price list exists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relationship builder with genuine credibility at senior level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong negotiator, comfortable with ambiguity and long sales cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent storyteller: can turn technical capability into a publisher-relevant revenue narrative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident, credible public speaker, comfortable on stage and in front of a room as a visible advocate for Awin’s strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starting and resilient. This is a build role, not a maintain role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and low-ego; comfortable pulling in engineering, legal, product and local market teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytically confident: fluent in performance data, able to interrogate reporting and defend a number.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic mindset paired with a bias to action and closing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technically literate rather than technical: able to hold a credible conversation about tags, tracking, CDNs and edge/worker deployments, page performance and data flows, and to know when to bring engineering into the room.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident with analytics and reporting platforms, including GA4, publisher analytics, BI dashboards and Excel or Sheets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with privacy and consent concepts, including GDPR and consent frameworks, as they affect publisher data sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English essential. German or another European language advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel to relevant markets as required&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
