&lt;p data-start=&quot;4798&quot; data-end=&quot;4942&quot; data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot; data-is-only-node=&quot;&quot;&gt;If you don’t meet 100% of the criteria, we still want to hear from you. Passion, curiosity, and impact orientation matter — tell us about yours.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;Who is Artefact?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact is a next-generation strategy and data consulting firm dedicated to transforming organisations through data and AI. We combine the rigour of top-tier strategy consulting with deep expertise in data, digital and analytics to help clients achieve tangible business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With 2,500+ consultants, data scientists and engineers, we work with global leaders such as Samsung, L’Oréal, Orange and Sanofi. Our Zurich office is at the heart of Artefact’s growth, advising clients on their most pressing strategic challenges — from AI strategy and governance to digital transformation roadmaps and new business model design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Main Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engagement Manager in our Zurich or Lausanne office, you will work at the intersection of strategy consulting and data and AI delivery. You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with client leadership teams to address high-stakes questions. How can AI reshape our business model? How should we govern and organise for data? Which strategic programmes deliver the most impact?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structured Problem-Solving:&lt;/strong&gt; Break complex challenges down into decisions a client can act on, combining consulting rigour with a working knowledge of what current AI can and cannot actually do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solution Design:&lt;/strong&gt; Turn a business question into a solution shape — what data it depends on, what kind of platform or product it should sit on, and what “good” looks like once it is built. You will do this alongside our data scientists and engineers, and you will be accountable for whether the design survives contact with production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; Run engagements end to end, from hypothesis framing and market and competitor analysis through to data maturity assessments, client workshops, governance design and implementation roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Feasibility &amp;amp; Economics:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the answer to &quot;will this work, and what will it cost&quot;. The evaluation approach, the unit economics per query or per case, and the point at which the business case stops closing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Engagement:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with C-level stakeholders and business unit leaders. You will build trusted relationships, communicate recommendations with clarity, and keep the work aligned to what the client is actually trying to decide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead mixed teams of consultants, data scientists and engineers. You are the person who can tell whether the technical plan is realistic, and the person the client believes when you say that it is.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge &amp;amp; Practice Building:&lt;/strong&gt; Contribute to the growth of Artefact&#39;s Zurich and Lausanne offices by shaping new offerings, creating intellectual capital - frameworks, thought pieces, benchmarks - and taking part in business development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Candidate Profile&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who can hold a technical position and a commercial one at the same time, and lead a team through both. The strongest candidates meet most of the following.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; A degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Data Science, Business, Economics or a related field. A strong technical foundation counts for more with us than where you studied.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Five to eight years across consulting and technology delivery, including at least one dedicated AI or data project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Acumen &amp;amp; AI Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; A strong dual affinity for business and technology. You have a deep working understanding of modern data and AI concepts — generative AI and LLMs, retrieval, predictive machine learning, cloud architectures — and of their practical business applications. You are capable of scoping AI use cases and of discussing technical constraints and opportunities confidently with C-level stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Depth:&lt;/strong&gt; You have owned the technical shape of AI work, not only its business case. You think in terms of enterprise architecture — how a solution fits the existing landscape, what it needs from data and governance, and how it scales from pilot to full rollout — and can defend those choices to technical and commercial stakeholders alike. You will not be writing production code, but you should have been close enough to it to be credible with the engineers with which you will collaborate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical &amp;amp; Problem-Solving Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong quantitative and analytical skills, and the judgement to know which number actually decides the question. You are comfortable getting to a defensible estimate with your assumptions stated out loud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Interpersonal Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Excellent written and verbal communication. You can take a technical trade-off to a non-technical sponsor without flattening it, and be challenged by an engineer without retreating into abstraction. You enjoy working in teams and in front of clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Languages:&lt;/strong&gt; Fluency in German/French and English, written and spoken, is strongly preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Eligibility:&lt;/strong&gt; You must be eligible to work in Switzerland.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy and the Build:&lt;/strong&gt; Artefact is neither a traditional strategy consultancy nor a pure technology player. You will move between the boardroom and the build, and be expected to be credible in both.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineers, not hand-offs:&lt;/strong&gt; Our 2,500 people include the data scientists and engineers you will work beside on the same engagement - not a delivery organisation you hand a slide deck to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zurich Office Impact:&lt;/strong&gt; As part of a growing Swiss team you will have visibility and impact from the first day. You will help shape Artefact&#39;s footprint in the region and work directly with senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning &amp;amp; Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; Regular training in both consulting method and AI and data capability, combined with international exposure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture of Doers:&lt;/strong&gt; Innovation, action, collaboration. We are entrepreneurial and fast-moving, committed to delivering impact while supporting each other&#39;s growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is based in &lt;strong&gt;Zürich or Lausanne&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Superchat, we&#39;re rebuilding how businesses talk to their customers. The phone call, the contact form, the support ticket: all of it is being replaced by messaging and AI. We&#39;re building the platform that runs underneath.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2020, Superchat has become the platform of choice for &lt;strong&gt;10,000+ businesses worldwide&lt;/strong&gt;, from globally recognized brands like Allianz, Auto1, Enpal, Danone, and GASAG to the small businesses, dental practices, and one-person startups that need to look bigger than they are. Today, &lt;strong&gt;millions of messages flow through Superchat every single day&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We started as a unified inbox: one place for every channel a customer might pick, WhatsApp, email, SMS, Instagram. Then ChatGPT happened, and the second chapter began: AI agents that respond across chat, email, and voice at the quality of the best human teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re &lt;strong&gt;100 people&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;profitable&lt;/strong&gt;, and have raised &lt;strong&gt;€18M in funding&lt;/strong&gt; (last round 4.5 years ago, we&#39;ve been growing on our own money since). Headquartered in Berlin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring our first Data Engineer to own Superchat&#39;s data platform end to end, from raw product and business data to the gold tables the whole company reports on. Our engineers have already built the foundations, including a warehouse, pipelines, dbt and reverse ETL. Now we need someone to make the platform trustworthy at scale, with testing, monitoring, clear modelling layers and customer history over time. You&#39;ll set the standards for how data is modelled and documented, and work with a Business Analyst to build the gold tables that Finance, Sales, Marketing and Product rely on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Want&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An experienced Data Engineer.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;You bring 3+ years of building and running data pipelines in production, ideally at a SaaS company. You&#39;ve owned a data platform, or a large part of one, and you&#39;re comfortable making the architecture calls yourself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong in SQL and dbt.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;You write and review complex SQL with ease. You&#39;ve built dbt projects with layered models, tests, documentation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At home in the Cloud.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;You have worked with Data Warehouses in the Cloud, ideally AWS Redshift. BigQuery or Snowflake is also fine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reliability-minded.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;You think in tests, freshness checks, idempotent loads and backfills. You want to know the data is wrong before a stakeholder tells you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curious about the business.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;You want to know what MRR, churn or an &quot;active workspace&quot; really mean, and you model data so those definitions hold everywhere they&#39;re used. Experience with subscription billing or product usage data is a plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Don’t Want&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pure dashboard builder.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;You&#39;d rather spend your days building dashboards and answering ad-hoc questions. That&#39;s our Business Analyst&#39;s job; yours is to build what they work from.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pure pipeline plumber.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;You move data from A to B but don&#39;t care what it means. Gold tables are only as good as the business understanding behind them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Over-engineer.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;You want Kafka, Spark and a lakehouse for data that fits comfortably in Redshift. We need pragmatic solutions that fit a 100-person company and can grow with it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote-only operator.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;You prefer fully remote work and don&#39;t want to build relationships in person. The data platform sits between many teams, and that works best with regular time together in our Berlin office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Data Stack&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Warehouse:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;AWS Redshift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ingestion:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Airbyte, custom Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transformation:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;dbt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Orchestration:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Dagster&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reverse ETL:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Hightouch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BI:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Metabase&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure &amp;amp; CI:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;AWS, Terraform, GitHub Actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Day To Day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own ingestion from our product database, Chargebee, HubSpot, Pipedrive, Intercom, Amplitude and other tools, using Airbyte where it works and your own Python where it doesn&#39;t.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build the dbt models that take raw data to gold tables, with clear layers, naming and documentation that the Business Analyst and the rest of the company can rely on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run orchestration in Dagster: schedules, dependencies, freshness checks and alerting, so a stalled sync gets noticed within hours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build data quality in: dbt tests, source checks and CI on every pull request.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture history where our source systems only keep the current state, so a question like &quot;which plan was this customer on last March?&quot; has an answer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the warehouse: Redshift performance and cost, access management, and AWS infrastructure in Terraform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the reverse ETL syncs (Hightouch) that send data back into HubSpot, Intercom and the other tools our teams work in.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Why People Choose Us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission that matters. &lt;/strong&gt;Real impact on small businesses, not abstract metrics&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Funded with conviction. &lt;/strong&gt;$18M raised and profitable&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Real ownership.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; You own the data platform end to end, not one step of someone else&#39;s pipeline&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid by design. &lt;/strong&gt;Our Berlin office in Prenzlauer Berg is the center of gravity, with two work-from-home days as the standard setup&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct feedback culture. &lt;/strong&gt;Honest, direct, and kind feedback is part of how we work together - in 1:1s, retrospectives, and everyday collaboration&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Choose between an Urban Sports Club/John Reed membership or a public transport/Dance subscription&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular company and team events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual personal development budget of €500 for conferences, courses, books, career coaching, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An inclusive and exciting startup culture that enables fast professional and personal growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Beautiful office in the heart of Berlin (Prenzlauer Allee 242) with free snacks, drinks, and top-notch equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We want to build a community, not just a company.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It’s important to us to create an environment where people genuinely enjoy spending time together - whether that’s through HYROX training, golfing, beer pong tournaments, running clubs, Warhammer, weekend activities, or whatever kind of community you’d like to help build here!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;re looking for people with passion, grit, and integrity. You&#39;re encouraged to apply even if your experience doesn&#39;t precisely match the description. At Superchat, we welcome diverse perspectives and people who think rigorously.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relocating to Berlin? We support you with practical relocation help. You&#39;ll feel home in no time.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We look forward to your application! 🙂&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;With your application you agree to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/f601741cb4f24d418411aa0ff86c3787?pvs=21&quot;&gt;privacy policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://i.imgur.com/Uicf3C7.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;800&quot; style=&quot;max-width: 100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GROPYUS is a technology-based construction company focused on building multi-story residential buildings. Thanks to its prefabricated building system with various design options, industrial offsite construction, and fully digitalized processes, the company manufactures aspirational, sustainable, and affordable homes using timber construction methods. GROPYUS is using scalable construction and manufacturing solutions to tap into a future market, boost Europe&#39;s strength in innovation, while also playing a substantial role in improving sustainability.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;job&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Senior Strategic Sourcing Manager (all genders) to help shape and scale our Procurement function in Berlin. You will establish and implement strategic procurement processes, build the first material group strategies and drive their end-to-end implementation. You will prepare and lead contract negotiations and contribute to the professionalisation and digitisation of Procurement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Material Groups in Scope:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Timber / CLT (cross-laminated timber) and related engineered wood products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Steel (structural steel, connectors, fasteners, profiles)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Windows / Façade systems (glazing, frames, façade elements, seals)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MEP (Mechanical, Electrical, Plumbing) including HVAC, electrical components, piping and sub-assemblies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;1) Build strategic procurement foundations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and implement strategic procurement processes (e.g., sourcing methodology, governance, templates, KPIs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the first material group strategies (category roadmaps, supplier landscape, TCO logic, risk and sustainability criteria) and drive implementation across the organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape supplier segmentation and SRM routines (performance reviews, development plans, risk mitigation).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure cross-functional alignment with Engineering, Production, Quality and Project teams to translate requirements into scalable sourcing strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;2) Lead sourcing &amp;amp; negotiations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own supplier discovery, RFx, benchmarking and award decisions for construction-material categories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and execute commercial and contractual negotiations (pricing, frameworks, terms &amp;amp; conditions) in collaboration with Legal/Finance and key stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive supplier qualification and continuous improvement with a focus on availability, quality, lead times, and total cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong partnerships across Europe and proactively manage supply risks (capacity, market volatility, compliance).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;3) Enable procurement professionalisation &amp;amp; digitisation (pick your impact lane)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on your strengths, you will own workstreams in one of the following areas to make Procurement scalable, transparent and data-driven.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and roll out scalable end-to-end processes (Source-to-Contract / Procure-to-Pay).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define roles, approvals and standards; develop playbooks and templates (RFx, negotiation, contract standards).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Analytics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build spend and category transparency; define a KPI framework (savings, supplier performance, delivery reliability, risk).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create decision-ready dashboards and routines for performance and savings tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Automation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify automation opportunities (workflows, approvals, master data, reporting) and drive implementation with tool owners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve data quality and process compliance through smart tooling and standardisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Change Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create change narratives, communication plans and training formats to ensure adoption of new processes and tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate workshops and enable stakeholders to work effectively with the new procurement set-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;5-7 years of experience in procurement consulting OR 7-10 years of professional expertise in strategic sourcing setting up and implementing material group and dual-sourcing strategies&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;with measurable impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong negotiation and contracting skills; structured, ownership-driven working style.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical mindset (TCO, supplier performance, risk) and ability to translate insights into action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident communicator, strong stakeholder management, and a collaborative approach in cross-functional set-ups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in both English and German (min. B2 level)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ERP/procurement systems (e.g., SAP S/4HANA) and data-driven procurement routines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of construction-material markets and supplier landscapes (timber/CLT, steel, windows/façade, MEP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How To Apply:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;Send us your CV and, if you like, a short note highlighting: (1) the categories/material groups you’ve owned, (2) negotiation and contracting experience, (3) examples of process build-up and/or digital procurement initiatives, and (4) your preferred impact lane (Process / Analytics / Automation / Change).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Be part of something big:&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;You’re here to make a change? Come on board. At GROPYUS, we are on a mission to re-think an entire industry. Join us in reinventing construction and sustainable, affordable living.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;It’s on you:&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;We offer a tremendous amount of ownership and room to make a mark - at all our organization levels. Find your solutions, drive and test them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Focus on results:&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;You choose if you work from home, a park, or the office. Whether you start your day early, after your run, or pick up on work when your kids are in bed. What counts is your contribution and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Bring your uniqueness to the team&lt;/em&gt;:&amp;nbsp;Innovation requires diversity of thought. Diversity in background, experience and thinking is crucial to create the best product for everyone. We actively seek diversity and strive to unlock each other’s full potential. We are very proud that people from all industries and all walks of life are joining our company – in addition to core areas such as construction, engineering, and start-ups, from stock-listed companies from across automotive e-Commerce, digital, sporting goods, and more. You will work in international teams with passionate colleagues. Inspire and be inspired.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Be an owner:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;Participate in the success of GROPYUS through stock options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Join us on our mission to design buildings as continuously evolving products to create the most exciting and affordable experience for all. We build for people and conserve the resources of our planet.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We can&#39;t wait to get to know you.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;For more information, visit our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gropyus.com/&quot;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;Are you excited by the challenge of strengthening the security of cloud platforms without slowing engineering teams down? We believe that real cloud security is about setting smart baselines, modeling threats early, and embedding guardrails directly into developer workflows, and we’re keen to hear about how you can help us implement this mentality&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About JetBrains&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We create intelligent software development tools for developers and teams. More than 15 million users, over 300,000 companies, and 88 of the Fortune Global Top 100 rely on our products to solve real, complex problems. Our mission is simple: make development teams more productive and AI adoptable at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our cloud footprint grows, we are investing heavily in the security of the platforms and products that support them. We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Product/Cloud Security Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to help us strengthen the security of the JetBrains Air platform and the services built on top of it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll take ownership of cloud and product security across our AWS and GCP environments. You’ll work directly on design choices, architecture reviews, and automation that reduce risk across the entire software development lifecycle. You’ll partner closely with platform engineering, SRE, and product teams to make secure choices the easiest path for developers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have substantial ownership and influence across teams while staying close to technical details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Day to day, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and continuously improve cloud security across JetBrains Air, including security posture, preventive controls, detection, and remediation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, maintain, and measure security baselines for AWS and GCP environments, covering IAM, networking, data protection, and workload configuration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate and evolve cloud security platforms and vulnerability-management solutions (e.g. Wiz, Orca Security, Upwind, Tenable, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish effective processes for triaging, prioritizing, assigning, and remediating cloud security findings and vulnerabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with platform engineering, SRE, and product engineering teams to design and implement practical security controls that fit naturally into developer workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform security design and architecture reviews for cloud services, APIs, and integrations. Conduct threat modeling and risk assessments to provide clear, actionable recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review product and platform changes for security implications throughout the entire software development lifecycle, from early design to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help improve security automation by integrating security checks, guardrails, and evidence into engineering and delivery pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support incident response, root-cause analysis, and drive systemic improvements that reduce recurrence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop meaningful metrics for cloud and product security, communicate trends and risks, and help prioritize security investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to security standards, guidance, runbooks, and patterns that make secure engineering easier across JetBrains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A pragmatic engineering mindset that balances security controls with developer velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong sense of ownership and the initiative to spot complex risks and address them early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, with the ability to explain technical trade-offs clearly to both engineers and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative mentality when working across distributed teams and engineering disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high bar for quality and a commitment to building sustainable, long-term security baselines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A curious and analytical approach to threat modeling and architectural risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established professional experience in security engineering or a closely related technical security domain, securing SaaS products or cloud-native services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with AWS and/or GCP security – specifically the ability to assess architecture and configurations directly, rather than relying solely on tool outputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience deploying, operating, or integrating cloud security and vulnerability-management platforms (e.g., Wiz, Orca Security, Upwind, Tenable).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with security architecture reviews, threat modeling, vulnerability management, and risk-based prioritization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of modern SaaS architectures (APIs, microservices, containers, Kubernetes, identity providers, networking, and managed cloud services).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with engineering, SRE, and product teams to translate security requirements into practical engineering solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and spoken English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building security automation or integrating security controls into CI/CD and infrastructure-as-code (IaC) workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Terraform or other IaC tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience securing Kubernetes-based platforms and containerized workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with detection engineering, cloud-native logging and monitoring, or security operations workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scripting or programming experience in Python, Go, Kotlin, Java, or a similar language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to SOC 2, ISO 27001, or other security and compliance frameworks for SaaS products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting customer-facing conversations about cloud, product, or platform security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, success means security is seamlessly integrated into how our platform and product teams build software. You’ll have established clear, measurable security baselines across our cloud infrastructure, reduced actionable security findings, and built strong trust with engineering teams so that threat modeling and security reviews happen naturally early in design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Why join JetBrains?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong base salary. We offer competitive pay that reflects your skills and experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible work location. Enjoy the freedom to work from home or from the office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote work. Spend up to 30 days per year working remotely from abroad.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extra time off. More days to relax, recharge, and do the things you love.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical insurance allowance. Enjoy peace of mind for you and your family&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and development opportunities. Access to conferences, courses, and language classes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relocation support. We help make your move as smooth and stress-free as possible.&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Language classes. Pick up the local language or sharpen your English skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fuel your day. Enjoy a hot meal or receive a lunch allowance on workdays.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health support. To help you feel your best, we provide easy access to professional mental health services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sports benefit. Enjoy an on-site gym or sports club stipend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internal events. Join company-wide celebrations and team gatherings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Some benefits may vary depending on location.&lt;/p&gt;
